# Simplicity and domain ownership

- Solve the current request. Do not add layers, abstractions, or features “just in case”.
- Before creating a file, look for the same flow (modal, service, mock). Reuse it.
- One domain, one owner: quotations in `quotationsService` + `NewQuotationForm`; clients in `clientsService` + `ClientFormModal`. Do not copy CRUD across modules.
- Business logic lives in `apps/web/src/services/*` (mock or NestJS HTTP via `VITE_API_MODE`).
- Prefer existing `apps/web/src/components/ui` and current forms. Avoid long files.
- Docs: English. UI copy and code comments: Spanish.
- Do not reintroduce quotation line-items, PocketBase at runtime, or npm — the repo is pnpm + mock/API.
- Backend: NestJS + MySQL in `apps/api`. Default UI is mock. No finance module.
- If you change a business flow, update only that section under `docs/operations/` (new ops docs in English).
